From 44b54cfcd10c5e66c484b27ee6f385069f89d656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fengjie <fengjie@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:06:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] deepin-port: fall back to input broker on SendInput soft
 failure

Wine's SendInput can return the full event count while setting last
error ERROR_INVALID_WINDOW_HANDLE (1400) once the Wine foreground
handle goes stale (e.g. after the GameViewer login window closes).
The previous check only fell back when result != count, so mouse
button events were silently dropped: the controller could move the
pointer but never click. Treat any nonzero error from the direct
call as a failure so the broker repairs focus or uses the direct
X11 injection route.
---
 src/uu_input_bridge.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/uu_input_bridge.c b/src/uu_input_bridge.c
index 225ea95..ed2794c 100644
--- a/src/uu_input_bridge.c
+++ b/src/uu_input_bridge.c
@@ -267,7 +267,13 @@ static UINT WINAPI bridged_send_input(UINT count, LPINPUT inputs, int size)
         result = original_send_input(count, inputs, size);
         error = GetLastError();
         direct_ms = (DWORD)(GetTickCount64() - direct_started_ms);
-        if (result != count) {
+        /* Wine can return the full count while still failing the injection:
+         * once the Wine foreground handle goes stale (for example after the
+         * GameViewer login window closes), SendInput reports result == count
+         * with last error ERROR_INVALID_WINDOW_HANDLE (1400) and drops mouse
+         * button events. Treat any nonzero error as a failure so the broker
+         * (relay focus repair or the direct X11 route) still receives it. */
+        if (result != count || error != ERROR_SUCCESS) {
             broker_started_ms = GetTickCount64();
             result = send_through_broker(count, inputs, size, &error);
             broker_ms = (DWORD)(GetTickCount64() - broker_started_ms);
